# NEGATIVE CONTROL for the gate: a mutation that genuinely goes red (it is MS1's edit),
# but names a catcher that will not fail. The gate MUST report MISATTRIBUTED and exit 1 —
# "something failed" is not evidence that the right thing failed.
#
# The named catcher does not exist in the suite, which is one way of being the WRONG
# catcher and the deterministic one: a real test might be dragged red by the same edit and
# turn this control into a CAUGHT. That is also why `negative-control: true` is required
# here — the specificity check forbids a catcher matching zero tests.
#
# RE-POINTED 2026-10-23: the old target `migrations/0005_verify_security_posture.sql` was
# deleted by the Supabase port (ADR-0015); the live posture migration is the file below,
# and this is byte-for-byte MS1's edit, which is observed CAUGHT in every gate run.
id: MS8
title: NEGATIVE CONTROL - a genuinely red mutation attributed to the wrong test
expect: caught
negative-control: true
expect-test: toolchain smoke runs a sync assertion
file: supabase/migrations/20261021140500_verify_security_posture.sql
count: 1
@@FIND
    where n.nspname in ('app','public') and has_function_privilege(g.grantee, p.oid, 'EXECUTE')
@@REPLACE
    where n.nspname in ('__never_a_schema__') and has_function_privilege(g.grantee, p.oid, 'EXECUTE')
@@END
